<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Windsor (1175)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1175</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Windsor (1175) was agreed between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a> and Ruaidrí Ua Conchobair, the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-king-of-ireland">High King of Ireland</a>, after the Anglo-Norman invasion. Ruaidrí accepted Henry as overlord and paid tribute, keeping Connacht and authority over Irish kings outside the Anglo-Norman lands of Leinster, Meath and the coastal towns. The settlement soon broke down as Anglo-Norman lords pushed further into Ireland.</p></div>
